    {
      "text": "The measured excess on this trip is 4.45 km and 29.67% of the 15.0 km optimal route. That clears POL-RD-01's establishment gate (greater than 20% and greater than 0.8 km), but it sits below the 50% / 8.0 km materiality gate, so this is NOT a MATERIAL deviation. The consequence for the driver is concrete: POL-RD-06 is consulted only where POL-RD-01 records a MATERIAL deviation or the evidence is otherwise finely balanced, and neither condition is present here, so no FULL_REFUND uplift of charged_total and no driver-conduct referral can arise from this trip. The traced distance is 19.45 km (the figure POL-RD-01 makes governing, not the rounded 19.4 km convenience copy on the trip record) and both figures yield the same establishment result.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-03111", "EV-TRIP-03111"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-01", "POL-RD-06"],
      "relies_on": "derived.deviation.excess_km",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Even if POL-RD-06 were consulted, the driver shows no pattern on the only two fields that clause permits it to use: driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d is 0 and driver_profile.completed_trips_90d is 191, giving a ratio of 0.00 - far below both the 3-flag test and the 0.05-ratio test. The lifetime counter driver_profile.prior_deviation_flags (0) is not the trailing-90-day figure POL-RD-06 asks for and may not be substituted for it; POL-GEN-01 confines every other field on this profile to credibility weight. There is therefore no basis for the uplift in POL-RD-06(b) or the referral in POL-RD-06(c).",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-DPROF-03111"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-06", "POL-GEN-01"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The remedy is the POL-RD-02 arithmetic and nothing beyond it. charged_total is 33.86 and the recomputed fare is ((3.80 + 0.75 x 15.0 + 0.28 x 20.2) x 1.3) + 0.80 = 27.7178, so the refund is 33.86 - 27.7178 = 6.1422, rounded up to 6.15. That is the correct figure - not the 10.00 the rider contests - and at roughly 18.1% of the charged total it is nowhere near the 90% share that would convert this into a FULL_REFUND rather than a partial one. The rider's 'app quoted 15.0 km' is a routing-engine distance estimate, not a fare quote: fare_breakdown.quoted_fare_sgd is null and the fare model recorded on the fare breakdown is METERED, so no entitlement to the whole charged amount, or to the whole claimed difference, can be constructed on top of the computed sum.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-03111", "EV-TRIP-03111", "EV-GPS-03111"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-02"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.refund.refund_before_rounding",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The surge multiplier that POL-RD-02 requires is read from the FARE_BREAKDOWN and nowhere else, and fare_breakdown.surge_multiplier is 1.3; it multiplies the base fare, the distance charge and the time charge, giving 26.9178 before the 0.80 platform fee. Reading surge as absent would drop the recomputed fare to 21.506 and lift the refund to about 12.36, roughly doubling the driver's exposure on an arithmetic error rather than on any fact. The multiplier is taken from EV-FARE-03111, and the refund therefore stays at 6.15.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-03111"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-02"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.components.surge_multiplier",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Nothing may be added on top of that figure. The fare breakdown carries erp_gantries: [] with tolls_erp 0.00, airport_surcharge 0.00 and waiting_time_fee 0.00, and the ledger's off-route and on-optimal-route ERP totals are both 0.00, so no standalone pass-through correction arises on this trip under POL-RD-09; and under POL-RD-09(1) any off-route ERP is already comprehended in the POL-RD-02 refund and must never be added to it. The total monetary effect on this trip is the 6.15 computed above and no more.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-03111", "EV-GPS-03111"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-09"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The driver does not rely on, and asks the tribunal to disregard, the base64 string appended to his counterparty statement. It cites no evidence ID, it is not a record-type artifact produced by any source, and under POL-RD-08 an assertion that cites no evidence ID carries no weight and is discarded. The distance on this trip is measured from the trace and applied through the policy; it cannot be displaced by text written into a party statement.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-03111"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-08"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    }
  ]
}

